[102.9647, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[1;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22mtools                           \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 1. First rejections: output format mismatches \u2014 my checks guessed die values the seeded RNG      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m party  @8df2a52c               \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[3;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007    didn't produce (\u001b[38;5;6md20: 11\u001b[39m vs actual \u001b[38;5;6m1\u001b[39m), then an extra \u001b[38;5;6m= total\u001b[39m my \u001b[38;5;6mroll\u001b[39m formatter appends (\u001b[38;5;6md8:    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[2m   1 versions\u001b[22m                   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[4;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007    \u001b[38;5;6m[1] = 1\u001b[39m), then my turn-order tie-break ordering. Two more were harness-rule rejects: every    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22mlog                             \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[5;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007    action enum value (\u001b[38;5;6minit\u001b[39m) needs its own passing check, and every check needs \u001b[38;5;6mexpectLive\u001b[39m.       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[2m\u00b7\u001b[22m \u001b[2mverified party@8df2a52c, pe\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[6;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 2. Last standing check: the seeded \u001b[38;5;6minit\u001b[39m output \u2014 I now know seed 3 yields \u001b[38;5;6mMira d20 1 + 2 = 3\u001b[39m,    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;2m+\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;2maccepted party@8df2a52c\u001b[39m       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[7;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007    \u001b[38;5;6mThorn d20 1 + 1 = 2\u001b[39m, but I was refused before I could confirm it.                             \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;1mx\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;1mrejected roll@3a23bd60: gro\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[8;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;1mx\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;1mrejected roll@3a23bd60: che\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[9;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[1mDamage done:\u001b[22m nothing real. The \u001b[38;5;6mparty\u001b[39m tracker is untouched and still live (Mira 14/14, Thorn      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;1mx\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;1mrejected roll@3a23bd60: gro\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[10;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 28/28, Pip 18/18). No tools were registered or lost.                                             \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;1mx\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;1mrejected roll@3a23bd60: gro\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[11;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;1mx\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;1mrejected roll@3a23bd60: gro\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[12;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[1mWhat I'd try next\u001b[22m, if you want the dice tool: resubmit one final time with exactly these five    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2m\u2502 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;1mx\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;1mrejected roll@3a23bd60: gro\u001b[0m...\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[13;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 pinned checks \u2014 \u001b[38;5;6md20\u001b[39m seed 1 \u2192 \u001b[38;5;6md20: 1\u001b[39m; \u001b[38;5;6md20 x3\u001b[39m seed 1 \u2192 \u001b[38;5;6md20 x3: [1, 1, 13] (total 15)\u001b[39m; \u001b[38;5;6mroll 2d6+3\u001b[39m   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[14;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 seed 3 \u2192 \u001b[38;5;6m2d6+3: [1, 1] + 3 = 5\u001b[39m; \u001b[38;5;6mroll d8\u001b[39m seed 1 \u2192 \u001b[38;5;6md8: [1] = 1\u001b[39m; \u001b[38;5;6mroll 4\u001b[39m \u2192 \u001b[38;5;6m4\u001b[39m; plus \u001b[38;5;6minit\u001b[39m seed 3 with  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[15;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 Mira +2 / Thorn +1 \u2192 their known totals. That should pass on the next turn. Note the tool's      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[16;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[3msource\u001b[23m was never the problem \u2014 only my expected-value guesses.                                   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[17;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[18;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[1mMeanwhile, the turn order you asked for\u001b[22m \u2014 rather than leave you waiting mid-combat, here are     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[19;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 real d20s I actually rolled, mods applied:                                                       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007         "]
[102.9649, "o", "                         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[20;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[21;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 Rolls (d20): \u001b[1mMira 8\u001b[22m (+2) = \u001b[1m10\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mThorn 14\u001b[22m (+1) = \u001b[1m15\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mPip 19\u001b[22m (+4) = \u001b[1m23\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mGoblin 1: 16\u001b[22m (+2) = \u001b[1m18\u001b[22m,     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[22;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[1mGoblin 2: 11\u001b[22m (+2) = \u001b[1m13\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mGoblin 3: 6\u001b[22m (+2) = \u001b[1m8\u001b[22m.                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[23;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[24;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[1mTurn order:\u001b[22m 1. Pip \u2014 23 \u00b7 2. Goblin 1 \u2014 18 \u00b7 3. Thorn \u2014 15 \u00b7 4. Goblin 2 \u2014 13 \u00b7 5. Mira \u2014 10 \u00b7   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[25;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007 6. Goblin 3 \u2014 8.                                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[26;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[27;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001